      "message": "fix(2d): Pass starts at (Auto/Inside/Outside) for 2D Offset\n\nA 2D Offset with an Outside containment cut each level core-first:\non the band between the stock reach and the part, the core is the\nmiddle of the band, so the first ring was a full slot in the stock.\n\nAdd the shared parameter machining2d::PassStart. The ring planner\n(waterline_passes) ranks its loops by family: Outside walks the outer\nboundary family from the boundary in, then the hole family from the\ncore back to its wall; Inside is the mirror; Auto is the old\nReverse(k) order, byte for byte. 2D Offset carries it as one OpParams\nfield (EditOperationParams, undo), one project key `pass_start`\n(auto is never written), the generic MCP edit_operation patch, a\ndigest write off Auto, and one Passes-tab row \"Pass starts at\".\nOther kinds and planners are not changed (Auto entry points).\n\nPinned by offset_pass_start (fig8.step, EM-0800-4FL, the reported\nheights) and the UI pass_start tests.\n\nFixes #3316\nRefs #3319\nRefs #1448\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
